WEBVTT

00:12.053 --> 00:14.389
♪ See the daylight ♪

00:15.223 --> 00:17.392
♪ Covering the sky ♪

00:18.852 --> 00:22.230
♪ Hear the wind say ♪

00:22.313 --> 00:26.484
♪ No matter what you do, my friend ♪

00:26.568 --> 00:29.696
♪ You know the world
Still needs your light ♪

00:29.779 --> 00:32.449
♪ Let it just shine ♪

00:32.532 --> 00:38.246
♪ You'll be free
From all the things you used to be ♪

00:40.040 --> 00:42.042
[distant bell clanging]

00:43.793 --> 00:48.298
DOONA!

00:50.050 --> 00:52.218
♪ You can't see anything now ♪

00:52.302 --> 00:54.095
[in Korean] ♪ Both your eyes are blinded ♪

00:54.179 --> 00:56.306
[in English] ♪ And you got no choices ♪

00:56.389 --> 00:58.058
[in Korean] ♪ I hypnotize you ♪

00:58.141 --> 01:02.062
[in English] ♪ Screaming out so loud ♪

01:02.145 --> 01:06.149
[in Korean] ♪ Screaming in my heart
Is the spell, love ♪

01:06.983 --> 01:09.903
[in English] ♪ I got this fire, fire… ♪

01:09.986 --> 01:11.738
- [music fades]
- [cameras clicking]

01:14.240 --> 01:15.408
[heartbeat]

01:24.125 --> 01:26.211
[somber music playing]

01:31.841 --> 01:33.843
[indistinct background chatter]

01:43.937 --> 01:44.771
[man] Doona.

01:45.522 --> 01:46.481
Lee Doona.

01:47.148 --> 01:48.191
Wake up.

01:49.400 --> 01:50.318
Lee Doona!

02:10.588 --> 02:12.298
[curious music playing]

02:12.382 --> 02:13.216
[sighs]

02:18.847 --> 02:23.726
EPISODE 2
GETTING TO KNOW EACH OTHER

02:30.900 --> 02:33.903
[Won-jun] Jeong-hun consumes
150 grams of protein a day.

02:36.030 --> 02:38.867
His sole concern is
the peace and well-being of his body.

02:38.950 --> 02:42.453
[woman] Straighten your elbows out,
make them taut. That's it. Now breathe in.

02:42.537 --> 02:44.205
[Won-jun] His dating views
are pretty rigid.

02:44.289 --> 02:46.207
Our population is out of control.

02:46.291 --> 02:48.126
It's not like propagation
is really needed.

02:48.209 --> 02:51.588
Our reproductive function in the future
should go through a degenerative process.

02:51.671 --> 02:54.132
That could be our next evolution.
Don't you think?

02:57.343 --> 02:58.469
Uh… [chuckles]

02:58.553 --> 03:00.889
Don't take any notice of him, babe.
He's an idiot.

03:00.972 --> 03:02.223
Say "ah."

03:02.307 --> 03:04.434
[Won-jun] Yun-taek's nickname
is the Hundred-Day Prince.

03:04.517 --> 03:05.685
- Right?
- [phone chimes]

03:05.768 --> 03:07.187
[Won-jun] He dreams of a fated love,

03:07.270 --> 03:10.565
but he can't ever go
more than 100 days without getting dumped.

03:11.774 --> 03:15.695
Of course, you won't always
know everyone's story entirely…

03:21.659 --> 03:23.661
[somber music playing]

03:30.585 --> 03:32.962
…because we all have
a version of ourselves

03:34.255 --> 03:36.090
that we want to hide from the world.

03:36.174 --> 03:37.258
[Doona sighs]

03:38.760 --> 03:39.677
Hmm?

03:49.520 --> 03:52.732
CONVENIENCE STORE

03:53.566 --> 03:54.692
[bystanders laughing]

03:55.777 --> 03:58.905
BLACK DEVIL GOLD

04:01.950 --> 04:04.160
[phone clicking]

04:04.994 --> 04:06.579
[register beeping]

04:06.663 --> 04:08.206
[mysterious music playing]

04:08.289 --> 04:09.249
[man] Hey there.

04:09.332 --> 04:11.876
I sent a screenshot of the message
the boss sent me yesterday.

04:11.960 --> 04:13.086
That's it, right?

04:13.836 --> 04:15.964
- Yeah, okay.
- [bell jangles]

04:21.052 --> 04:21.970
Uh…

04:22.929 --> 04:23.763
Hey!

04:23.846 --> 04:24.722
[bus approaching]

04:29.727 --> 04:30.561
Mmm.

04:40.321 --> 04:41.281
EDWARD

04:41.364 --> 04:44.242
[man] So you'll go by Edward here.
We all go by English names.

04:44.325 --> 04:46.911
We really lucked out
you were available for hire so soon.

04:47.954 --> 04:49.122
Oh, look, there's Alice.

04:50.540 --> 04:51.708
[Jin-ju] No way!

04:52.542 --> 04:55.878
- Seriously, you're the new guy?
- [man] Do you two know each other?

04:57.255 --> 04:58.840
Uh, yeah! [laughs]

05:00.591 --> 05:01.634
What a coincidence.

05:02.635 --> 05:03.636
Welcome aboard.

05:04.262 --> 05:05.596
[Jin-ju laughs]

05:06.514 --> 05:08.099
[gentle music playing]

05:08.182 --> 05:10.143
- [woman] Morning!
- [Won-jun] Hello, welcome.

05:10.226 --> 05:12.520
- Can I have one iced Americano, please?
- [Won-ju] Certainly.

05:12.603 --> 05:14.689
Mister, your iced hazelnut latte is ready.

05:15.189 --> 05:16.024
One moment.

05:16.107 --> 05:17.567
Enjoy your latte.

05:18.484 --> 05:19.777
[woman] Thank you so much.

05:23.448 --> 05:24.907
[register beeping]

05:27.201 --> 05:28.703
[gentle music continues]

05:32.957 --> 05:35.376
- Oh!
- [laughs]

05:40.715 --> 05:41.674
[sighs]

05:47.513 --> 05:48.765
[footsteps approaching]

05:48.848 --> 05:50.058
LEE DOONA
MISSED CALL

05:51.476 --> 05:52.477
Ah, that's cold!

05:52.977 --> 05:54.103
[Jin-ju chuckles]

05:54.187 --> 05:55.980
- Here you go.
- Oh, thanks so much.

06:01.361 --> 06:03.905
[Jin-ju sighs] Ah, this is nice.

06:06.741 --> 06:07.742
[Jin-ju sighs]

06:10.703 --> 06:12.121
[Won-jun] You make good coffee.

06:12.205 --> 06:14.248
- [Jin-ju] It's good, right?
- [Won-jun] Mm-hmm.

06:14.332 --> 06:15.291
[Jin-ju] Hmm.

06:16.292 --> 06:19.253
MARCH 2021 MOCK EXAM SCHOLARSHIP
1ST PLACE YANGJIN HIGH SCHOOL LEE WON-JUN

06:19.337 --> 06:21.422
2ND PLACE
YANGJIN GIRLS' HIGH SCHOOL KIM JIN-JU

06:21.506 --> 06:22.924
[sentimental music playing]

06:27.053 --> 06:28.471
KIM JIN-JU
YANGJIN GIRLS' HIGH

06:35.311 --> 06:37.355
[Kooksu] Oh? There's Kim Jin-ju.

06:37.438 --> 06:38.689
Do you know her?

06:38.773 --> 06:41.067
Uh, our restaurant's
in her family's building.

06:41.150 --> 06:43.152
They are super-duper rich.

06:43.653 --> 06:46.614
- Ah.
- Oh! Yu-i is there. [chuckles]

06:47.198 --> 06:49.117
Hey, I'll go say hi. I'll be back.

06:50.118 --> 06:50.993
[Kooksu chuckles]

06:52.829 --> 06:54.288
[girl] Oh, got it!

06:54.372 --> 06:55.289
[girls laughing]

06:55.957 --> 06:57.125
[Jin-ju] Okay, got it.

06:57.625 --> 06:59.377
- [laughing]
- [girl] Yeah!

06:59.460 --> 07:01.003
[game beeping]

07:05.216 --> 07:07.051
[rain pattering]

07:07.135 --> 07:08.094
[Jin-ju] Excuse me.

07:08.177 --> 07:09.053
Hmm?

07:09.137 --> 07:11.139
- Oh!
- So I heard you're good with math.

07:11.222 --> 07:12.723
- Is that right?
- [Won-jun] Mm-hmm.

07:12.807 --> 07:14.976
[Jin-ju] Do you think
you could help me with this?

07:20.648 --> 07:21.524
[Won-jun] Mmm…

07:22.483 --> 07:23.651
[Jin-ju sighs] Oh.

07:24.360 --> 07:25.319
- Oh.
- [Jin-ju] Here.

07:25.403 --> 07:26.237
Thank you.

07:27.780 --> 07:29.782
So, um, this triangle here…

07:33.536 --> 07:34.454
- [horn honks]
- … cosine…

07:37.540 --> 07:38.749
Are you going home now?

07:39.250 --> 07:41.711
Uh, no. I'm heading to a tutoring gig.

07:41.794 --> 07:42.879
Oh.

07:43.921 --> 07:45.631
[Jin-ju] I work a lot, huh?

07:46.215 --> 07:48.342
You're not going through
any troubles now, are you?

07:48.968 --> 07:50.803
Why? You worried my family's going broke?

07:50.887 --> 07:52.388
No, no, no, that's not why.

07:53.389 --> 07:54.682
Well, I'm glad everything's good.

08:04.066 --> 08:04.901
[Won-jun] Oh.

08:14.410 --> 08:17.330
ALICE

08:20.041 --> 08:21.167
[sighs]

08:22.376 --> 08:23.753
[woman on TV] Whenever I have tuna,

08:23.836 --> 08:27.173
I always kind of feel like
I've made it in life, you know?

08:27.256 --> 08:29.550
So I'm gonna lay down a bed of rice,

08:29.634 --> 08:33.554
and then I'll put this
in a fermented tuna chopsticks…

08:33.638 --> 08:34.805
Wait, what did I say?

08:35.389 --> 08:37.850
- Now I have to warn you…
- [phone ringing]

08:37.934 --> 08:40.603
So salty that you
really only have to add a tiny amount.

08:40.686 --> 08:41.729
MOM

08:41.812 --> 08:43.940
[woman on TV]
Next, you're gonna take some of this.

08:44.023 --> 08:44.899
[phone clatters]

08:46.400 --> 08:49.445
Kind of like making sushi.
Well, that's what it feels like.

08:49.529 --> 08:52.073
Use a little
of the sesame-oil-and-salt mixture too.

08:52.657 --> 08:54.158
I was really craving this today.

08:54.242 --> 08:56.702
I wanted to have it
with warm, cooked rice.

09:03.292 --> 09:04.210
[sighs]

09:06.337 --> 09:07.171
[TV beeps]

09:11.592 --> 09:13.594
[emotional music playing]

09:19.517 --> 09:20.977
[line ringing]

09:21.060 --> 09:22.436
[phone vibrating]

09:26.816 --> 09:28.484
DOONA

09:29.277 --> 09:32.697
[automated voice] Sorry, the number you're
trying to reach is currently unavailable.

09:32.780 --> 09:35.575
Please leave a message after the tone.

09:45.585 --> 09:49.213
[man] Didn't we agree
you wouldn't keep a personal cell phone?

09:50.006 --> 09:53.134
Sometimes I just wanna hear your voice,
you know?

09:57.138 --> 09:58.806
[man] Don't cause any trouble.

10:04.353 --> 10:05.938
- [door beeps]
- [Won-jun chuckles]

10:06.022 --> 10:07.815
[clicking tongue]

10:07.898 --> 10:09.692
[Won-jun] Aw, you're so cute.

10:09.775 --> 10:11.193
[chuckles]

10:11.277 --> 10:12.403
You like me, don't you?

10:12.486 --> 10:13.404
[cat meows]

10:13.946 --> 10:15.489
Just be careful with people.

10:15.573 --> 10:17.533
You're better off
staying out of their way.

10:17.617 --> 10:19.368
Lots of bad people out there.

10:20.411 --> 10:21.579
- Hmm?
- [cat snarls]

10:21.662 --> 10:23.122
Ah! [winces]

10:23.205 --> 10:27.543
Ah. Wow, you're a genius.
You understood me right away.

10:27.627 --> 10:28.794
I'm sorry I scared you.

10:29.420 --> 10:31.213
- I'm sorry.
- [cat meows]

10:32.757 --> 10:34.967
- [Doona] Are you hurt?
- [Won-jun] Hmm?

10:41.515 --> 10:44.310
- [Doona] You're bleeding.
- It doesn't hurt at all. I'm all right.

10:47.438 --> 10:48.564
Where were you?

10:49.231 --> 10:50.524
I called you earlier.

10:50.608 --> 10:51.525
At my new job.

10:51.609 --> 10:52.443
So you were tutoring?

10:52.526 --> 10:55.571
No, at a café.
I haven't gotten a tutoring job yet.

11:00.201 --> 11:02.662
Do you know the thing
that I really hate the most? Take a guess.

11:03.663 --> 11:06.332
- Uh, horrible singing?
- Ding!

11:07.750 --> 11:09.293
Ignoring my phone calls.

11:12.505 --> 11:13.839
So how can I say it?

11:15.132 --> 11:16.926
It makes me feel abandoned.

11:18.886 --> 11:22.264
- It really sucks.
- Oh, uh, I'm sorry. I didn't mean to.

11:22.348 --> 11:24.725
[Doona chuckles]

11:26.686 --> 11:28.771
I wasn't talking about you, actually.

11:30.064 --> 11:31.273
You should rest.

11:33.150 --> 11:34.235
Um, your phone call…

11:34.318 --> 11:37.905
So, uh, why exactly did you call?
Was there something wrong earlier?

11:40.324 --> 11:42.284
Well, I was just hoping
to hear your voice.

11:43.369 --> 11:46.122
- So next time, you should answer my call.
- Hmm.

11:46.205 --> 11:48.582
[emotional music playing]

12:11.480 --> 12:13.816
[keypad beeping]

12:13.899 --> 12:15.109
[door beeps]

12:16.610 --> 12:18.154
[door closes, beeps]

12:22.241 --> 12:24.243
[inaudible]

12:27.413 --> 12:28.539
[phone vibrates]

12:32.460 --> 12:36.005
[woman] Hello, and welcome to the 44th
Civil Engineering Student Association.

12:36.088 --> 12:38.466
To kick off the new semester,
the Civil Engineering…

12:38.549 --> 12:40.968
[Won-jun] Due to a study group
meeting, I will not be…

12:41.051 --> 12:43.763
[woman] 20,000 won to attend,
50,000 won to decline.

12:47.308 --> 12:48.517
[Won-jun] I will attend.

12:56.734 --> 12:58.068
START-OF-TERM PARTY!

12:58.152 --> 12:59.278
[cheering]

12:59.361 --> 13:00.863
- What's our school?
- Minsong!

13:00.946 --> 13:02.448
- Our department?
- Engineering!

13:02.531 --> 13:03.574
[girl] What's our class?

13:03.657 --> 13:04.533
- Civil!
- We are civil!

13:04.617 --> 13:06.619
- Hey! Hey! Hey!
- [girl] Civil! Engineering! Civil!

13:06.702 --> 13:07.620
- Let me hear it!
- Hey!

13:07.703 --> 13:09.580
- We are number one!
- [cheering]

13:25.888 --> 13:28.265
This quarter's results overseas

13:28.349 --> 13:31.852
depend entirely on
the 2022 KCON JAPAN performance.

13:31.936 --> 13:35.147
The single showcase after KCON JAPAN
will be our largest showcase ever.

13:35.231 --> 13:38.526
[man] We plan to expand the media showcase
to the scale of a full concert.

13:38.609 --> 13:41.904
- [woman] Of the international artists…
- [man] Doona. Lee Doona.

13:41.987 --> 13:44.031
[woman vocalizing]

13:52.331 --> 13:53.207
[sighs]

14:07.263 --> 14:09.849
[boy] Hey, take some of this
chaser with your shot, okay?

14:09.932 --> 14:10.808
[phone vibrating]

14:10.891 --> 14:12.351
[boy] What's with your expression?

14:13.143 --> 14:14.103
Hey!

14:14.186 --> 14:15.604
LEE DOONA

14:15.688 --> 14:17.690
[clattering]

14:19.275 --> 14:20.776
That's not good enough! Let go!

14:21.277 --> 14:24.154
Hey, if you're sorry, then drink this.
Yeah? You were wrong? You're sorry?

14:24.238 --> 14:26.031
All right. Hey, sit down.

14:26.949 --> 14:27.783
Um, hello?

14:28.284 --> 14:29.743
[Doona] Hell-low or hell-high?

14:30.452 --> 14:32.204
Wow. That was a bad dad joke!

14:32.288 --> 14:33.205
[Doona laughs]

14:34.123 --> 14:36.458
Where are you? Right now I'm in the area.

14:37.042 --> 14:38.752
[boy] Hey there, how are you?

14:40.045 --> 14:42.840
You're the pretty chick I saw
at school the other day, right?

14:42.923 --> 14:44.550
- Come on. Give it back.
- Stop it.

14:46.302 --> 14:48.053
Come on. Stop ignoring me
and say something.

14:48.137 --> 14:50.431
- [Won-jun] Please give it back.
- [boy] Hello? Anybody there?

14:50.514 --> 14:52.641
[Won-jun] Hey, cut it out
and give me back my phone!

14:54.685 --> 14:58.063
- What the hell are you looking at, huh?
- [Doona] Hey, you!

14:59.481 --> 15:01.942
[dramatic rock music playing]

15:04.111 --> 15:05.112
[sighs]

15:08.866 --> 15:10.200
[Doona] Did he hit you?

15:10.284 --> 15:11.201
[Won-jun] Not yet.

15:13.787 --> 15:15.915
How dare you put your hands on my Won-jun?

15:16.498 --> 15:17.917
So what year are you?

15:18.709 --> 15:20.336
Get your dirty hands off me, kid.

15:20.419 --> 15:22.922
You think 'cause you're pretty
you can do what the fuck you want?

15:23.005 --> 15:24.590
You're starting to piss me off.

15:24.673 --> 15:27.718
Is that right, you total dipshit?
So what are you gonna do about it, huh?

15:27.801 --> 15:30.054
You should worry more
about what I'm gonna do to you.

15:30.137 --> 15:31.847
- [Won-jun] Hey, hey, wait.
- [boy] Go for it.

15:32.848 --> 15:35.059
Do it, then. [laughs]

15:35.142 --> 15:37.269
Huh? Huh? Go for it, chick.

15:37.353 --> 15:38.479
Go right on ahead.

15:38.562 --> 15:39.939
[tense rock music playing]

15:40.022 --> 15:41.440
[man] Don't cause any more trouble.

15:41.523 --> 15:42.733
[sighs]

15:42.816 --> 15:45.402
[boy] I thought you were pissed,
so just hit me already, huh?

15:45.986 --> 15:47.947
If you can't do it,
stop waving that thing around.

15:48.030 --> 15:49.740
- You think that I can't?
- [boy] Just do it!

15:52.618 --> 15:53.786
[glass shatters]

15:56.580 --> 15:58.540
[boy breathing shakily]

15:59.416 --> 16:00.960
[Won-jun panting]

16:02.294 --> 16:03.295
[sighs]

16:10.970 --> 16:13.597
PHARMACY

16:21.188 --> 16:22.022
[Won-jun] Ah.

16:22.106 --> 16:22.940
[winces]

16:25.401 --> 16:26.235
Ah! [winces]

16:26.318 --> 16:28.195
- Ah.
- [bell jangles]

16:30.489 --> 16:31.365
[sighs]

16:41.291 --> 16:42.543
I don't need to drink that.

16:42.626 --> 16:44.878
I should drink it.
I'm the one who really needs it.

16:52.302 --> 16:53.429
Hmm. Take it.

16:55.014 --> 16:57.599
You can't go around hitting people
over the head with glass bottles.

16:57.683 --> 16:59.852
You'll get arrested immediately.
All right?

16:59.935 --> 17:01.395
He said to do it, didn't he?

17:13.949 --> 17:15.951
Look, I don't know
what your life story might be,

17:16.535 --> 17:19.204
um, but if you need to go
to anger management, uh…

17:20.205 --> 17:22.916
There are resources available for you
if you need treatment.

17:23.834 --> 17:24.835
[chuckles]

17:25.669 --> 17:27.796
Why? Do you think I've been through a lot?

17:27.880 --> 17:29.840
- Uh… uh, well…
- Uh-huh?

17:29.923 --> 17:32.009
Normally girls don't walk around the city

17:32.092 --> 17:34.219
with glass bottles
to smash people's heads in.

17:35.137 --> 17:36.972
I wanted to have a drink with you.

17:38.474 --> 17:40.225
I bought it from the beverage store.

17:45.189 --> 17:46.690
Let's grab a drink, Doona.

17:47.441 --> 17:48.525
What's stopping us?

17:52.112 --> 17:54.573
[indistinct chatter]

17:57.201 --> 17:58.327
Huh?

17:59.203 --> 18:01.872
- Oh, yay!
- [indistinct chatter]

18:01.955 --> 18:04.750
- [Jin-ju] Ah, how about fried chicken?
- Okay, fried chicken for you.

18:04.833 --> 18:08.212
- [laughs]
- [girl] This is gonna be so fun.

18:08.295 --> 18:10.464
Fried chicken and beer sounds delicious.

18:10.547 --> 18:13.092
- Wait, how many are we?
- [girl 2] I'm literally starving now.

18:13.175 --> 18:14.009
I can't wait.

18:14.093 --> 18:15.636
[girl 3] I wasn't hungry before.

18:15.719 --> 18:17.805
- Wait here. I'm just gonna go say hi.
- Oh, sure.

18:18.388 --> 18:20.307
Won-jun! [chuckles]

18:21.183 --> 18:23.560
- Were you here for the party?
- Uh-huh. You too?

18:23.644 --> 18:24.812
Mm-hmm.

18:25.562 --> 18:27.564
- [Jin-ju] Oh, you're with someone.
- Uh, yeah.

18:27.648 --> 18:30.442
We, uh… we live in the same co-ed house.

18:30.526 --> 18:31.610
- She, uh--
- Oh!

18:32.152 --> 18:34.321
Lee Doona?! Is that you?

18:34.404 --> 18:36.615
Hey, Kook Su-jin is a superfan, isn't he?

18:37.491 --> 18:38.617
I'm a fan too.

18:41.328 --> 18:43.247
- Let's get going. I'm pretty tired.
- [gasps]

18:43.330 --> 18:48.210
Oh! Um, I'm sorry,
but by any chance, do you drink at all?

18:48.293 --> 18:50.170
- You can join us.
- How about another time?

18:50.254 --> 18:53.173
And why would I let
a complete stranger drink with me, again?

18:53.715 --> 18:55.801
- [Jin-ju and Doona] Cheers!
- [Won-jun] Cheers!

18:55.884 --> 18:57.886
[curious music playing]

19:00.305 --> 19:01.598
- [Doona] I'm…
- [Jin-ju sighs]

19:02.391 --> 19:03.475
Well, I'm…

19:04.393 --> 19:05.561
I'm honestly

19:07.062 --> 19:08.313
just a shy girl.

19:08.397 --> 19:10.732
- Really shy, actually.
- Hmm.

19:11.358 --> 19:13.360
[laughs]

19:14.528 --> 19:16.363
You're so lucky though, you know that?

19:16.446 --> 19:18.699
I'm serious! You're lucky!

19:18.782 --> 19:19.908
[laughs]

19:19.992 --> 19:20.826
That's right!

19:22.035 --> 19:23.662
And, yeah, like, um…

19:23.745 --> 19:27.291
Well, I… I'm the kind of girl
everyone likes, huh?

19:27.374 --> 19:29.126
[laughing]

19:30.711 --> 19:32.296
Hey, I bet he does too!

19:33.255 --> 19:34.381
Hey, Won-jun.

19:35.257 --> 19:36.967
Uh, you still do, right?

19:37.050 --> 19:40.679
- Um… well, um…
- [Doona] Who cares if he does or doesn't?

19:40.762 --> 19:42.139
It's not really important.

19:43.223 --> 19:46.476
Hey, Jin-ju.
We should just get married, right?

19:46.560 --> 19:48.979
[Jin-ju] Okay, Doona, yeah,
I do wanna marry you.

19:49.062 --> 19:51.732
- [Doona] Yeah, let's get married!
- [Jin-ju] Let's get married!

19:51.815 --> 19:53.525
[laughing]

19:53.609 --> 19:56.904
Hey, Jin-ju, I think you might
have already missed the subway train.

19:56.987 --> 19:58.322
No, we're tying the knot!

19:58.405 --> 20:01.325
Yeah, quiet, we have to tie the knot!

20:01.408 --> 20:03.327
[laughing]

20:03.911 --> 20:05.913
[Won-jun] I think
you missed the last train.

20:06.413 --> 20:07.331
Hmm.

20:07.998 --> 20:09.082
[Doona] Hey.

20:10.250 --> 20:13.420
- Jin-ju, crash at my house tonight, huh?
- [gasps]

20:13.503 --> 20:16.173
- Actually, you should just live here.
- [gasps]

20:17.174 --> 20:18.425
You get all of this.

20:18.926 --> 20:21.970
- I will give you everything--
- I really needed a place to stay, Doona!

20:22.554 --> 20:24.181
- Thank you!
- [Doona laughs]

20:24.264 --> 20:26.183
Jin-ju, you're crazy for real.

20:26.266 --> 20:27.601
Hey. [laughs]

20:28.727 --> 20:30.687
Wait, are you crazy?

20:31.855 --> 20:33.815
Yeah, you must be crazy!

20:35.067 --> 20:36.443
Hey, wake up, Jin-ju.

20:36.526 --> 20:38.904
- [phone vibrating]
- Are you asleep now?

20:39.529 --> 20:40.364
DAD

20:40.447 --> 20:42.032
Hey, why are you sleeping?

20:42.616 --> 20:44.117
- [Won-jun] Oh.
- [Jin-ju] You're crazy.

20:44.618 --> 20:46.703
Jin-ju, wake up.
Your father's calling you right now.

20:46.787 --> 20:48.705
- Jin-ju?
- What's going on?

20:48.789 --> 20:50.707
Oh, what should we do?
We can't just let it ring.

20:50.791 --> 20:51.917
Well, answer the phone.

20:52.000 --> 20:53.543
It'd be really bad if a man answered.

20:54.461 --> 20:56.046
[Doona laughs]

20:56.755 --> 20:59.258
You're a man, huh? [laughs]

20:59.341 --> 21:01.802
- Oh, he's a man!
- Ah, what do I do?

21:03.053 --> 21:05.931
- Huh? Oh, no, you really shouldn't answer.
- Um, yes? Hello?

21:11.061 --> 21:12.813
Oh, yes, hello, Mr. Kim?

21:12.896 --> 21:14.106
Why yes, you're so intuitive.

21:14.189 --> 21:15.899
I'm Lee Se-na,
a friend of your daughter's.

21:15.983 --> 21:17.734
We're in literature together.

21:17.818 --> 21:20.487
The start-of-term party
finished a little late tonight,

21:20.570 --> 21:22.489
so she made the decision to stay here.

21:23.573 --> 21:24.574
Oh, Jin-ju is…

21:24.658 --> 21:28.161
She's, um, just in the shower now.
Should I have her call you?

21:29.454 --> 21:32.291
Oh, yes, everything's fine.
Don't worry about her.

21:32.374 --> 21:35.919
Oh, yes, of course. Both my parents
are here in the house. Yes, sir.

21:36.795 --> 21:39.006
I sure will. You have a great night, sir.

21:43.093 --> 21:45.721
Wow, you were so perfect,
like a total natural.

21:45.804 --> 21:47.472
- That was awesome to see.
- Cool.

21:47.556 --> 21:50.726
[chuckles] You should've been
an actor instead, not a pop star.

21:55.939 --> 21:56.815
[sighs]

21:59.985 --> 22:01.695
I'm going for a cigarette now.

22:02.696 --> 22:04.197
You should go home, all right?

22:05.032 --> 22:06.158
[grunts quietly]

22:11.872 --> 22:12.873
[groans]

22:16.043 --> 22:17.002
[sighs]

22:22.257 --> 22:23.383
Go home, I said.

22:23.467 --> 22:26.553
Uh, Yun-taek told me
not to come home before 2:00.

22:27.387 --> 22:28.430
So I will in a little.

22:33.143 --> 22:34.019
Oh.

22:40.609 --> 22:41.693
[Doona sighs]

22:42.903 --> 22:43.820
[Won-jun] Hmm.

22:53.330 --> 22:55.749
What's with your hand?
It's looking pretty rough now.

22:56.249 --> 22:57.292
What?

22:58.043 --> 23:01.588
Ah. It's weird, but I seem
to get injured every time I'm around you.

23:02.923 --> 23:04.591
Maybe we're not meant to hang out.

23:05.092 --> 23:05.967
[Doona sighs]

23:07.052 --> 23:08.553
She's pretty, and you know it.

23:09.471 --> 23:10.514
Jin-ju.

23:11.807 --> 23:13.934
Hmm. She really is.

23:18.271 --> 23:20.232
[sighs] I'm jealous of that.

23:23.026 --> 23:25.904
Wait. Her being pretty
makes you feel jealous?

23:28.240 --> 23:30.117
No, I'm jealous of you.

23:33.036 --> 23:35.497
You have
this really great relationship with her,

23:36.498 --> 23:38.333
'cause you've known her so long.

23:38.917 --> 23:40.127
That's why I'm jealous of you.

23:43.171 --> 23:44.297
[groans]

23:46.800 --> 23:48.301
It's so not fair, you know.

23:50.929 --> 23:53.432
I have yet to know
a true friend like that.

23:54.933 --> 23:56.768
Oh! Hey, Doona, be careful.

23:56.852 --> 23:58.854
You've had a lot to drink, remember? Ah.

23:59.855 --> 24:02.732
I sometimes wonder
how I ended up like this in life.

24:06.987 --> 24:08.321
[Won-jun] Oh!

24:47.944 --> 24:49.863
You're adorable, you know that?

24:50.655 --> 24:52.324
I almost messed up and did it.

24:52.949 --> 24:54.075
Almost did what?

24:54.159 --> 24:57.204
So if you can manage it,
next time you should turn away.

24:59.998 --> 25:00.874
Hmm.

25:04.794 --> 25:05.754
Mm-mm.

25:14.930 --> 25:15.805
[sighs]

25:24.439 --> 25:27.108
[Won-jun] Hey, Doona, be careful.
You've had a lot to drink, remember?

25:27.192 --> 25:28.652
Oh!

25:31.154 --> 25:32.447
[faucet running]

25:32.531 --> 25:33.365
Ah.

26:08.400 --> 26:10.527
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY JOB FAIR

26:19.286 --> 26:20.120
Uh…

26:20.870 --> 26:22.289
I, uh… I promised washed it.

26:22.872 --> 26:25.041
That's strange.
It still has your smell on it.

26:25.125 --> 26:26.918
I guess it's your fabric softener.

26:29.713 --> 26:31.548
So, did you get home all right yesterday?

26:31.631 --> 26:34.092
Doona said she didn't know
when you had left this morning.

26:34.175 --> 26:36.595
- So when did you head out?
- Oh man, that's right.

26:37.095 --> 26:39.723
I forgot to thank Doona
for letting me sleep over last night,

26:41.141 --> 26:43.143
because somebody had me in shock.

26:43.226 --> 26:44.060
Who?

26:44.686 --> 26:47.480
Won-jun, hey, it's me.
You don't need to hide it.

26:48.273 --> 26:49.232
I saw you guys.

26:50.483 --> 26:52.861
You and Doona kissed. I saw it all.

26:52.944 --> 26:55.238
[spluttering] Kiss? Uh, you did?

26:55.322 --> 26:56.990
Uh-huh! [chuckles]

26:57.532 --> 26:59.576
Oh, Se-hun's here. I'm over here!

27:00.410 --> 27:02.996
- I should go. I'll see you at work, okay?
- [Won-jun] Oh.

27:03.079 --> 27:04.623
Uh, I didn't kiss her…

27:08.960 --> 27:10.003
But I… [sighs]

27:17.469 --> 27:18.928
I didn't kiss her.

27:20.555 --> 27:21.598
[glass clinking]

27:29.064 --> 27:30.023
[sighs]

27:36.321 --> 27:37.906
This is a milk container.

27:40.200 --> 27:41.910
Cosmetics are general waste.

27:43.495 --> 27:47.749
I guess your manager did this for you.
You obviously haven't had to do it before.

27:47.832 --> 27:49.167
[items clatter]

27:50.085 --> 27:51.294
You sound irritated.

27:51.378 --> 27:52.796
Is it because you're hangry?

27:54.047 --> 27:56.299
Or is because Jin-ju rejected you?

27:56.383 --> 27:59.386
Huh? What has she got to do
with any of this? Jeez, come on.

28:00.845 --> 28:02.097
And this is plastic.

28:02.722 --> 28:04.265
You got rejected. Bingo.

28:05.725 --> 28:07.519
I wasn't rejected, okay?

28:08.311 --> 28:10.605
She thinks you and I
have something going on right now.

28:10.689 --> 28:12.315
Hmm? She does?

28:12.399 --> 28:13.858
[chuckles] Why?

28:13.942 --> 28:16.903
Because she saw us that night that, um,

28:17.529 --> 28:18.446
on the roof,

28:18.530 --> 28:20.240
well, uh… yeah.

28:21.324 --> 28:22.742
Ah.

28:25.328 --> 28:26.955
You should've set her straight.

28:28.081 --> 28:31.876
Okay, whatever. It's not like
we're together or anything, right?

28:31.960 --> 28:34.254
Trying to explain it
would just make it more awkward.

28:34.337 --> 28:36.089
So what do we do now?

28:36.172 --> 28:38.091
Should we just date for real, then?

28:38.717 --> 28:39.551
[gasps]

28:40.135 --> 28:43.054
Just so you know, it's very clear to me
now why you don't have friends.

28:50.061 --> 28:51.020
[Won-jun sighs]

28:51.855 --> 28:52.939
And what makes you say that?

28:53.022 --> 28:57.527
Well, you have no filter when you speak.
You say whatever you're thinking.

28:57.610 --> 28:59.487
There aren't many people like that.

28:59.571 --> 29:02.824
From what I'm seeing, you don't care
what anyone thinks about you.

29:02.907 --> 29:04.701
And you don't feel the need to hold back.

29:05.493 --> 29:06.745
In some ways, I envy you.

29:08.246 --> 29:09.414
Huh? What the heck?

29:09.998 --> 29:11.499
This is also general waste.

29:15.128 --> 29:15.962
Uh-huh.

29:16.713 --> 29:17.589
Yeah.

29:18.715 --> 29:22.260
I do whatever the fuck I want
regardless of what anyone says. So what?

29:22.844 --> 29:23.762
Is that bad? Huh?

29:23.845 --> 29:25.096
Uh… uh…

29:25.180 --> 29:26.055
Ah, I get it now.

29:26.139 --> 29:28.391
I'm alone because of my attitude,
is that it?

29:28.475 --> 29:29.726
It's all on Doona!

29:29.809 --> 29:32.312
I can't possibly fix my career now.
So what? So what?

29:32.395 --> 29:34.939
I should just stick to selling
weight-loss pills on social media?

29:35.023 --> 29:37.400
- Is that what you think, huh?
- Doona, I never said that.

29:37.484 --> 29:40.612
I'm gonna sort the recycling
however the fuck I want, okay?

29:40.695 --> 29:43.239
Don't tell me
where the fuck to put stuff, you hear?

29:54.542 --> 29:55.627
[sighs]

30:07.889 --> 30:09.849
[man] You couldn't just keep it together.

30:14.145 --> 30:15.271
[inhales]

30:20.860 --> 30:21.820
[sighs]

30:23.279 --> 30:24.197
[sighs]

30:24.280 --> 30:27.242
[man] Has it occurred to you
that you brought this upon yourself?

30:54.519 --> 30:55.353
[sighs]

31:01.150 --> 31:02.110
[Won-jun] Hey, Kooksu.

31:02.193 --> 31:04.153
You know that girl Doona you love
from Dream Sweet

31:04.237 --> 31:05.697
or whatever they're called?

31:06.197 --> 31:08.783
[Kooksu] Yes! The goddess Doona!
Yeah, why?

31:08.867 --> 31:10.493
[Won-jun] Is she
going through a hard time?

31:10.577 --> 31:13.371
I hear a lot of celebrities deal with
mental illness and stuff like that.

31:13.454 --> 31:15.415
Maybe she struggled with cyberbullying?

31:15.498 --> 31:16.791
[Kooksu] Oh, no way, dude!

31:16.875 --> 31:18.918
Doona just does
whatever the hell she wants to,

31:19.002 --> 31:20.003
and that's how she is.

31:20.086 --> 31:23.131
Yeah, she just left the band to focus on
her studies for now, so I hear.

31:23.214 --> 31:25.216
Please only pay attention to facts
from now on.

31:25.300 --> 31:27.719
- But is that a fact?
- [Kooksu] Dude, trust me.

31:27.802 --> 31:30.388
But, hey, why you asking about my girl?

31:30.972 --> 31:32.974
- [Won-jun] But it's not a fact?
- Wait, are you a fan?

31:33.057 --> 31:34.517
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

31:34.601 --> 31:36.352
I just thought about her randomly.

31:36.853 --> 31:39.898
Yeah. I, too,
have thought about her a whole lot.

31:39.981 --> 31:41.566
In fact, I think about her all the time.

31:41.649 --> 31:42.859
Yeah, how much is that?

31:42.942 --> 31:43.776
What?

32:20.188 --> 32:21.022
[sighs]

32:21.522 --> 32:23.274
[gentle piano music playing]

32:45.129 --> 32:47.590
What? Got something to say?

32:47.674 --> 32:50.385
Uh, mm-mm…

32:52.971 --> 32:54.013
Wait, have you eaten yet?

32:58.017 --> 33:00.770
Actually, I cooked way too much food
for dinner just now.

33:01.771 --> 33:03.731
If you haven't eaten,
give me a minute, okay?

33:03.815 --> 33:06.317
- Wait here. I'll bring it down to you.
- Wait, don't.

33:29.048 --> 33:30.299
[Won-jun grunts]

33:30.383 --> 33:31.926
- Hey.
- [Won-jun] Hmm?

33:32.010 --> 33:34.762
Don't you know it's a rule to give notice
before you bring a guest over?

33:34.846 --> 33:37.473
I didn't exactly bring her over just now.

33:38.516 --> 33:41.144
- So, she actually lives right below us.
- [Yun-taek] Exactly!

33:41.853 --> 33:44.981
Instead, why don't you give notice
about how antisocial you are

33:45.064 --> 33:46.274
so the poor girl can dodge you?

33:46.858 --> 33:48.860
[Yun-taek chuckles]

33:49.944 --> 33:52.071
Pay no attention
to this heartless jerk, okay?

33:52.155 --> 33:57.118
And, uh, come visit us
anytime you want to, hmm? Okay?

34:12.425 --> 34:14.927
Can I, um…
can I ask you a personal question?

34:15.845 --> 34:18.139
Uh… and don't feel like
you have to answer me.

34:18.723 --> 34:20.600
Mm-hmm. Fire away.

34:21.684 --> 34:22.852
Why did you quit Dream Sweet?

34:27.440 --> 34:30.234
Maybe I haven't accomplished
enough in life to get it, hmm,

34:30.985 --> 34:33.780
but I can't imagine someone
who's worked as hard as you

34:34.280 --> 34:35.698
just giving up on it.

34:37.867 --> 34:40.703
Sorry. You must get
these kinds of questions all the time.

34:41.996 --> 34:44.832
Actually, you're the first one to ask me.

34:45.500 --> 34:46.584
Oh, really?

34:47.168 --> 34:50.088
In my experience, I find that people
will believe what they want to.

34:50.171 --> 34:52.256
They don't care to know the actual truth.

34:56.719 --> 34:57.595
[sighs]

34:57.678 --> 34:59.013
But if I had to be honest…

35:01.015 --> 35:02.809
there wasn't a reason why I quit.

35:04.977 --> 35:06.562
I just unexpectedly…

35:09.774 --> 35:10.942
couldn't sing at all anymore.

35:12.777 --> 35:13.945
The end, hmm?

35:25.748 --> 35:26.749
[cat meows]

35:32.839 --> 35:34.173
Do you have any change?

35:36.634 --> 35:38.136
[Won-jun] All right. Good luck.

35:39.846 --> 35:41.389
[Doona] Here I go…

35:41.472 --> 35:44.100
- [machine beeping]
- [Doona] Ah!

35:45.726 --> 35:48.229
- Oh! [laughs]
- [Won-jun] Oh! Oh!

35:48.729 --> 35:50.356
- [squeals]
- Ah.

35:53.151 --> 35:54.235
[machine beeps]

35:55.444 --> 35:57.321
- [Doona] Ah! Oh.
- [Won-jun] Oh. Oh.

35:57.405 --> 35:59.574
- Ah.
- Ah, seriously?! No!

35:59.657 --> 36:01.826
- [Won-jun] Oh! Oh!
- [Doona squeals]

36:02.827 --> 36:03.661
[groans]

36:07.081 --> 36:08.583
- Really? All of this?
- [Doona] Mm-hmm.

36:12.837 --> 36:13.880
Hurry up. I need it!

36:14.589 --> 36:15.506
Here you go.

36:15.590 --> 36:16.757
[machine beeps, whirs]

36:20.011 --> 36:21.012
[machine beeping]

36:21.804 --> 36:23.472
[Doona] Oh! Oh!

36:25.850 --> 36:27.977
Oh! [squeals]

36:28.060 --> 36:30.062
[crowd cheering]

36:33.149 --> 36:34.609
You should've kept it together.

36:35.693 --> 36:38.237
Now go back out there and sing.
We'll talk after.

36:42.200 --> 36:44.535
[woman in Japanese] Dream Sweet,
you're on in three minutes!

36:44.619 --> 36:45.786
We're starting now!

36:45.870 --> 36:47.788
[in English]
I don't think I can sing tonight.

36:47.872 --> 36:49.373
What do you mean you can't sing?

36:49.874 --> 36:51.500
My anxiety is through the roof.

36:53.336 --> 36:55.463
You're going on stage… no matter what.

36:56.172 --> 36:58.507
Enough of your nonsense.
Now, get out there.

37:04.555 --> 37:06.098
[man in Japanese] Ten seconds!

37:10.353 --> 37:11.354
Five seconds!

37:11.437 --> 37:13.147
Four. Three.

37:13.231 --> 37:14.440
Two.

37:15.733 --> 37:17.401
[machine whirs]

37:21.155 --> 37:22.782
[crowd cheering]

37:22.865 --> 37:24.533
[rock music playing]

37:41.926 --> 37:43.803
[cheering continues]

37:45.471 --> 37:47.473
[pop music playing]

37:53.646 --> 37:55.356
[in English] ♪ Stop this game ♪

37:55.439 --> 37:57.108
♪ Wait for it ♪

37:57.191 --> 38:01.570
[in Korean]
♪ I now appear before your eyes ♪

38:01.654 --> 38:03.155
[in English] ♪ Whisper spell ♪

38:03.239 --> 38:04.782
♪ You can't escape ♪

38:04.865 --> 38:07.201
♪ I got you ♪

38:07.285 --> 38:08.536
[in Korean] ♪ Come to me ♪

38:09.120 --> 38:11.414
[in English]
♪ You can't see anything now ♪

38:11.497 --> 38:12.999
[in Korean] ♪ Your eyes are blinded ♪

38:13.082 --> 38:15.584
[in English] ♪ And you got no choices ♪

38:15.668 --> 38:16.961
[in Korean] ♪ I hypnotize you ♪

38:17.670 --> 38:21.257
[in English] ♪ Screaming out so loud… ♪

38:21.841 --> 38:24.385
[man] Hey, Lee Doona!
You really let yourself go!

38:27.221 --> 38:29.098
[man] Can you bite on this
just once for me?

38:29.181 --> 38:30.224
♪ Fire! ♪

38:30.308 --> 38:33.936
♪ You make it burning, burning, burning ♪

38:38.149 --> 38:39.483
[woman] You have to make a point?

38:39.567 --> 38:41.444
Ugh! Seriously?!

38:42.987 --> 38:45.239
You wanna be a diva?
Leave it for your solo career.

38:47.908 --> 38:49.243
[cameras clicking]

38:52.747 --> 38:54.248
A CERTAIN BIG STAR IS SUPER RUDE

38:54.332 --> 38:55.624
[Doona] This is plagiarism!

38:55.708 --> 38:57.835
They're obviously identical
down to the composition!

38:57.918 --> 39:00.546
Hey, you!
You're gonna lose everything and end up

39:00.629 --> 39:03.215
selling weight loss pills on social media!

39:07.261 --> 39:08.262
[thud]

39:08.804 --> 39:10.931
- [indistinct chatter]
- [woman 3] Did something happen?

39:11.015 --> 39:13.267
[woman 4] What's wrong with her?
What's happening on stage?

39:13.351 --> 39:15.353
[dramatic music playing]

39:21.942 --> 39:23.069
[man] Doona.

39:23.152 --> 39:24.320
Lee Doona!

39:25.196 --> 39:26.364
Wake up.

39:27.490 --> 39:28.449
[echoes] Lee Doona!

39:36.749 --> 39:39.418
Whoo! I did it! Oh! [squeals]

39:39.502 --> 39:41.504
[laughing]

39:43.297 --> 39:44.215
[squeals]

39:44.715 --> 39:46.384
[chuckles]

39:47.468 --> 39:48.886
- Let's go!
- [Won-jun] Okay.

39:51.055 --> 39:52.014
[Won-jun claps]

39:59.814 --> 40:03.109
- Today was my birthday, you know.
- Ah, seriously?

40:03.609 --> 40:06.487
And I happened to make
birthday seaweed soup? Wow.

40:07.947 --> 40:09.573
You should eat better, you know?

40:09.657 --> 40:11.283
Food makes everything better
in my opinion.

40:11.367 --> 40:13.661
Although I don't have
much going on in my life,

40:14.245 --> 40:18.082
I find that eating well can really,
uh, um, boost my morale these days.

40:22.586 --> 40:23.546
So what's the deal?

40:24.213 --> 40:26.132
What's the story between Jin-ju and you?

40:28.634 --> 40:32.430
Well, I think that's
how things go with high-school crushes.

40:33.431 --> 40:36.183
Like a fool, you begin to read
way too much into every little detail.

40:36.809 --> 40:39.770
First it's despair. Then you're floating
in the clouds sometimes no reason.

40:39.854 --> 40:41.647
[sighs] Then you overdo it,

40:42.815 --> 40:44.775
and things end up falling apart, right?

40:47.903 --> 40:51.073
- You're sure she doesn't have feelings?
- Yes, I'm sure, Doona.

40:51.157 --> 40:52.324
I think you're wrong.

40:52.408 --> 40:53.409
How do you know?

40:53.492 --> 40:56.078
- Never mind that. You could court her.
- And how would I do that?

40:56.871 --> 40:58.539
You make her heart race.

40:59.748 --> 41:01.876
Girls like Jin-ju wanna feel like that.

41:02.460 --> 41:04.920
You should put her against the wall.

41:05.504 --> 41:06.338
[chuckles]

41:06.422 --> 41:09.383
Just think about it.
Push her up against any wall.

41:09.467 --> 41:12.553
Then look at her
and don't even say a single word to her

41:12.636 --> 41:13.804
for ten seconds.

41:14.305 --> 41:16.640
No, you won't need ten. Five is plenty.

41:16.724 --> 41:17.808
[sighs]

41:17.892 --> 41:19.101
And then…

41:20.603 --> 41:22.480
What? And then what?

41:26.817 --> 41:28.152
You come up with the next part.

41:29.236 --> 41:31.030
I can't do everything for you, huh?

41:32.114 --> 41:33.657
Won-Jun, you're so demanding.

41:35.117 --> 41:36.076
[chuckles]

41:37.786 --> 41:39.580
You could always practice with me.

41:40.206 --> 41:41.499
And I'll tell you

41:41.582 --> 41:43.459
if my heart starts racing.

41:44.126 --> 41:45.044
[chuckles]

41:45.628 --> 41:46.629
Uh…

41:46.712 --> 41:47.713
[sighs]

42:02.895 --> 42:04.396
Happy birthday to you.

42:08.400 --> 42:11.070
[chuckles] See?
I'm not good at that this at all, right?

42:11.153 --> 42:12.112
[chuckles]

42:13.781 --> 42:16.700
Let's get going.
It's late, and your birthday is over, hmm?

42:35.261 --> 42:37.263
[gentle emotional music playing]

42:39.932 --> 42:40.933
[door closes]

42:42.101 --> 42:44.061
[chuckles]

42:58.367 --> 42:59.201
[gasps]

43:02.663 --> 43:03.956
[line ringing]

43:10.170 --> 43:11.213
[gasps]

43:11.297 --> 43:14.258
Uh, it's me. Were you already sleeping?

43:16.176 --> 43:17.011
[Jin-ju] No.

43:19.346 --> 43:21.181
Why? You have something to say?

43:21.807 --> 43:24.059
Um, yeah, well, um, just so you know,

43:24.143 --> 43:26.353
there's nothing between Doona and I, okay?

43:26.437 --> 43:28.439
I think you had the wrong idea earlier,

43:28.522 --> 43:31.483
um, and well, I hope
that makes things more clear.

43:34.278 --> 43:35.154
[Jin-ju] Oh yeah?

43:37.114 --> 43:37.948
All right.

43:39.742 --> 43:40.576
[sighs]

43:42.328 --> 43:43.287
[Jin-ju] I'm glad.

43:45.539 --> 43:47.541
[emotional music playing]

43:50.669 --> 43:52.796
[man] Happy birthday. I'll be in touch.

43:53.714 --> 43:55.716
[dramatic music playing]

44:07.311 --> 44:08.228
[Doona gasps]

44:12.650 --> 44:14.693
[panting]

44:23.077 --> 44:24.328
[car horn honks]

44:31.710 --> 44:32.795
[car horn honks]

44:33.295 --> 44:36.048
[panting]

44:42.638 --> 44:44.264
